language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Capital budgeting: choose a set of investments, each with a cash outflow and a net present value, so that the total cash outflow stays within the budget and the total net present value is maximised.
given cash_flow_dim1 : int
letting n = cash_flow_dim1
given budget : int
given cash_flow : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int
given npv : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool
find z : int(0..sum(npv))

branching on [x]
maximising z
such that
$ the sum of all chosen investments must not exceed the budget (cash outflow of each investment taken when chosen)
(sum i : int(1..n) . x[i] * cash_flow[i]) <= budget,
$ the total NPV z is the sum of the NPVs of the chosen investments
z = (sum i : int(1..n) . x[i] * npv[i])
